#### Problem 1: Tight Coupling Creates Fragile Integrations

**Current State**:

```csharp
// Gainwell claims service tightly coupled to state MMIS API
public class ClaimsSubmissionService
{
    private readonly IStateMmisClient _stateMmisClient;

    public async Task<SubmissionResult> SubmitClaimToStateAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        try
        {
            // Synchronous call to state MMIS - blocking
            var response = await _stateMmisClient.SubmitClaimAsync(
                new StateClaimRequest
                {
                    ClaimId = claim.Id,
                    ProviderId = claim.ProviderId,
                    MemberId = claim.MemberId,
                    ServiceDate = claim.ServiceDate,
                    BilledAmount = claim.BilledAmount
                },
                timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));

            if (response.IsAccepted)
            {
                await UpdateClaimStatusAsync(claim.Id, "Submitted");
                return SubmissionResult.Success(response.ConfirmationNumber);
            }
            else
            {
                await UpdateClaimStatusAsync(claim.Id, "Rejected");
                return SubmissionResult.Rejected(response.Errors);
            }
        }
        catch (HttpRequestException ex)
        {
            // State MMIS unavailable - claim submission fails
            _logger.LogError(ex, "State MMIS unavailable");
            return SubmissionResult.Failed("State system temporarily unavailable");
        }
        catch (TaskCanceledException ex)
        {
            // State MMIS timeout - claim submission fails
            _logger.LogError(ex, "State MMIS timeout");
            return SubmissionResult.Failed("State system timeout");
        }
    }
}
```

**Impact**:
- **Fragile Dependencies**: Gainwell operations depend on state MMIS availability; state system downtime = Gainwell claims processing down
- **Cascading Failures**: State API slowness causes Gainwell API timeouts, affecting providers
- **Coordinated Deployments**: State API changes require immediate Gainwell updates
- **Version Lock-In**: Can't upgrade until all connected systems coordinate

**Business Consequence**:
- Extended state MMIS maintenance windows can force claims processing offline, affecting provider submissions
- Integration projects can be delayed when external systems change APIs without notice
- Significant support costs for integration-related incidents

