#### Problem 3: No Standard Integration Pattern

**Current State**:

Each Gainwell product team implements integrations differently:

```csharp
// Team A: Direct HTTP calls with custom retry
public class TeamAIntegration
{
    public async Task<T> CallExternalApiAsync<T>(string endpoint)
    {
        for (int retry = 0; retry < 3; retry++)
        {
            try { return await _httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<T>(endpoint); }
            catch { await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(retry * 2)); }
        }
        throw new IntegrationException("Failed after retries");
    }
}

// Team B: Message queue with custom protocol
public class TeamBIntegration
{
    public async Task PublishToPartnerAsync(object data)
    {
        var message = JsonSerializer.Serialize(data);
        await _serviceBus.SendAsync("partner-queue", message);
    }
}

// Team C: File-based with SFTP
public class TeamCIntegration
{
    public async Task SendFileToPartnerAsync(string filePath)
    {
        using var sftp = new SftpClient(_config.Host, _config.Username, _config.Password);
        sftp.Connect();
        sftp.UploadFile(File.OpenRead(filePath), $"/inbound/{Path.GetFileName(filePath)}");
    }
}
```

**Impact**:
- **Inconsistent Patterns**: Each team solves same problems differently
- **Code Duplication**: Retry logic, error handling, authentication duplicated
- **Maintenance Burden**: No shared libraries or frameworks
- **Knowledge Silos**: Integration expertise trapped in individual teams

**Business Consequence**:
- Estimated 40% code duplication across integration implementations
- New partner integration takes 3-6 months due to lack of reusable components
- Security vulnerabilities in custom integration code (2022 security incident)

