#### Variation 4: Bidirectional Event Exchange with Correlation

**Scenario**: Request-response pattern using events (e.g., prior authorization request/decision)

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Outbound: Publish prior auth request event
public async Task RequestPriorAuthorizationAsync(PriorAuthRequest request)
{
    var correlationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

    await _eventBus.PublishAsync(new PriorAuthRequestedEvent
    {
        EventId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
        CorrelationId = correlationId,
        EventType = "com.gainwell.priorauth.requested.v1",
        OccurredAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
        Data = new
        {
            RequestId = request.Id,
            MemberId = request.MemberId,
            ProviderId = request.ProviderId,
            ServiceCode = request.ServiceCode,
            Justification = request.ClinicalJustification
        }
    });

    // Store correlation for matching response
    await _correlationStore.SaveAsync(new Correlation
    {
        CorrelationId = correlationId,
        RequestId = request.Id,
        RequestedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
        ExpiresAt = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(7)
    });
}

// Inbound: Receive prior auth decision event from payer
public class PriorAuthDecisionConsumer : IConsumer<PriorAuthDecisionEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<PriorAuthDecisionEvent> context)
    {
        var evt = context.Message;

        // Find original request using correlation ID
        var correlation = await _correlationStore.GetByCorrelationIdAsync(evt.CorrelationId);

        if (correlation == null)
        {
            _logger.LogWarning("Received orphaned prior auth decision: {EventId}", evt.EventId);
            return;
        }

        // Update prior auth with decision
        await _priorAuthService.RecordDecisionAsync(correlation.RequestId, new Decision
        {
            IsApproved = evt.Data.IsApproved,
            DenialReason = evt.Data.DenialReason,
            ApprovedUnits = evt.Data.ApprovedUnits,
            ValidThrough = evt.Data.ValidThrough,
            ReceivedAt = DateTime.UtcNow
        });

        // Publish internal event for other systems
        await context.Publish(new PriorAuthDecisionReceivedEvent
        {
            RequestId = correlation.RequestId,
            Decision = evt.Data
        });
    }
}
```

**When to Use**: Request-response workflows; need to correlate related events; multi-step business processes

**Trade-offs**:
- **Pros**: Maintains loose coupling with async pattern; handles long-running processes; supports timeouts
- **Cons**: More complex correlation logic; must handle orphaned responses; eventual consistency

