### Example 1: State MMIS Claim Submission Integration

**Scenario**: California MMIS requires all claim adjudication data for payment processing and reporting. Previously used synchronous API calls causing frequent timeouts and integration delays.

**Before (Synchronous Integration)**:

```csharp
public class ClaimsService
{
    private readonly IStateMmisClient _stateClient;

    public async Task AdjudicateClaimAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        // Adjudicate claim locally
        var result = await _adjudicationEngine.ProcessAsync(claim);

        // Synchronous call to state MMIS - BLOCKING
        try
        {
            await _stateClient.SubmitAdjudicatedClaimAsync(new StateClaim
            {
                ClaimId = claim.Id,
                AdjudicatedAmount = result.ApprovedAmount,
                DenialReason = result.DenialReason,
                AdjudicationDate = DateTime.UtcNow
            });
        }
        catch (HttpRequestException ex)
        {
            // State MMIS down - what to do?
            // Option 1: Fail claim adjudication (bad UX)
            // Option 2: Queue for retry (custom retry logic)
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to submit claim to state MMIS");
            throw; // Adjudication fails if state is down
        }

        await SaveClaimAsync(claim, result);
    }
}
```

**Problems**:
- Claims processing blocked when state MMIS unavailable (6-hour incident affected 25,000 claims)
- Timeout handling scattered across codebase
- No visibility into delivery status
- Manual intervention required for failed submissions

**After (Event-Driven Integration)**:

```csharp
public class ClaimsService
{
    private readonly IEventBus _eventBus;

    public async Task AdjudicateClaimAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        // Adjudicate claim locally - NO EXTERNAL DEPENDENCY
        var result = await _adjudicationEngine.ProcessAsync(claim);

        // Save claim result
        await SaveClaimAsync(claim, result);

        // Publish event - fire and forget
        await _eventBus.PublishAsync(new ClaimAdjudicatedEvent
        {
            EventId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
            EventType = "com.gainwell.claims.adjudicated.v1",
            CorrelationId = claim.CorrelationId,
            OccurredAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            Data = new
            {
                ClaimId = claim.Id,
                MemberId = claim.MemberId,
                ProviderId = claim.ProviderId,
                AdjudicatedAmount = result.ApprovedAmount,
                DenialReason = result.DenialReason,
                AdjudicationDate = DateTime.UtcNow,
                LineItems = claim.LineItems.Select(li => new
                {
                    ServiceCode = li.ServiceCode,
                    ApprovedAmount = li.ApprovedAmount
                })
            }
        });
    }
}

// Integration Gateway handles delivery separately
public class ClaimEventAdapter : IConsumer<ClaimAdjudicatedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<ClaimAdjudicatedEvent> context)
    {
        var evt = context.Message;

        // Get all partners subscribed to claim events
        var partners = await _partners.GetSubscribedPartnersAsync(evt.EventType);

        foreach (var partner in partners)
        {
            // California MMIS via SFTP
            if (partner.Id == "state-ca-mmis")
            {
                await DeliverViaSftpAsync(evt, partner);
            }
            // Other states may use webhooks or different protocols
        }
    }
}
```

**Outcomes**:
- **Zero claim processing downtime** during state MMIS outages (events queued automatically)
- **Improved delivery success rate** to state MMIS compared to synchronous approach
- **Reduced claim adjudication latency** through asynchronous processing
- **Reduced support costs** from handling failed integrations
- Automatic retry handles transient failures without manual intervention

