### Example 3: Payer-to-Payer Data Exchange (Bidirectional Events)

**Scenario**: CMS mandates payer-to-payer data exchange when members switch plans. Medicaid MCO needs to send member history to commercial payer, receive acknowledgment.

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Outbound: Send member history when member disenrolls
public async Task SendMemberHistoryToPriorPayerAsync(string memberId, string priorPayerId)
{
    var correlationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

    // Gather member data (claims, care plans, medications)
    var memberHistory = await _memberHistoryService.CompileHistoryAsync(memberId);

    // Publish member history event
    await _eventBus.PublishAsync(new MemberHistoryRequestedEvent
    {
        EventId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
        CorrelationId = correlationId,
        EventType = "com.gainwell.member.history.requested.v1",
        OccurredAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
        Data = new
        {
            MemberId = memberId,
            TargetPayerId = priorPayerId,
            HistoryPeriod = new { Start = DateTime.UtcNow.AddYears(-2), End = DateTime.UtcNow },
            DataTypes = new[] { "Claims", "CarePlans", "Medications", "Encounters" },
            MemberHistory = memberHistory  // FHIR Bundle
        }
    });

    // Store correlation for tracking response
    await _correlationStore.SaveAsync(new Correlation
    {
        CorrelationId = correlationId,
        RequestType = "MemberHistoryExchange",
        PartnerId = priorPayerId,
        RequestedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
        ExpiresAt = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(7)
    });
}

// Inbound: Receive acknowledgment from payer
public class MemberHistoryAcknowledgmentConsumer : IConsumer<MemberHistoryAcknowledgedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<MemberHistoryAcknowledgedEvent> context)
    {
        var evt = context.Message;

        // Find original request
        var correlation = await _correlationStore.GetByCorrelationIdAsync(evt.CorrelationId);
        if (correlation == null)
        {
            _logger.LogWarning("Received orphaned acknowledgment: {EventId}", evt.EventId);
            return;
        }

        // Update exchange status
        await _dataExchangeService.RecordAcknowledgmentAsync(new Acknowledgment
        {
            CorrelationId = evt.CorrelationId,
            PartnerId = evt.Source.PayerId,
            Status = evt.Data.Status,  // Received, Processed, Error
            RecordsReceived = evt.Data.RecordsReceived,
            ProcessedAt = evt.Data.ProcessedAt,
            ErrorMessage = evt.Data.ErrorMessage
        });

        // Publish internal event for audit
        await context.Publish(new MemberDataExchangeCompletedEvent
        {
            MemberId = correlation.MemberId,
            PartnerId = evt.Source.PayerId,
            Status = evt.Data.Status
        });
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- **Asynchronous workflow** - no timeout issues with large member histories
- **Correlation tracking** - link requests and acknowledgments
- **Audit trail** - complete record of data exchanges for CMS compliance
- **Retry handling** - automatic retry if payer temporarily unavailable

**CMS Compliance**:
- HL7 FHIR US Core profiles for all member data
- Delivery within 24 hours of member disenrollment
- Complete audit log of exchange attempts and acknowledgments
- Support for data corrections via compensating events

