### Example 4: Pharmacy Network Integration (High-Volume Events)

**Scenario**: Real-time pharmacy claim adjudication through NCPDP network. 500,000+ pharmacy claims/day requiring <2 second adjudication.

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Inbound: Receive pharmacy claim from PBM
[ApiController]
[Route("api/integration/pharmacy")]
public class PharmacyClaimController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpPost("claims")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitPharmacyClaimAsync(
        [FromBody] NcpdpClaimRequest ncpdpClaim)
    {
        var correlationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

        // Transform NCPDP to internal event
        var claimEvent = new PharmacyClaimReceivedEvent
        {
            EventId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
            CorrelationId = correlationId,
            EventType = "com.gainwell.pharmacy.claim.received.v1",
            OccurredAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            Data = TransformNcpdpToInternal(ncpdpClaim)
        };

        // Publish to high-throughput topic
        await _eventBus.PublishAsync("pharmacy-claims", claimEvent);

        // Return correlation ID for response matching
        return Accepted(new { correlationId, status = "processing" });
    }

    // Pharmacy polls for adjudication results
    [HttpGet("claims/{correlationId}/result")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> GetAdjudicationResultAsync(string correlationId)
    {
        var result = await _resultCache.GetAsync(correlationId);

        if (result == null)
        {
            return NotFound(new { status = "processing" });
        }

        // Transform internal result to NCPDP response
        var ncpdpResponse = TransformInternalToNcpdp(result);
        return Ok(ncpdpResponse);
    }
}

// Pharmacy adjudication service consumes claims
public class PharmacyAdjudicationService : IConsumer<PharmacyClaimReceivedEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<PharmacyClaimReceivedEvent> context)
    {
        var evt = context.Message;

        // Adjudicate claim (eligibility, formulary, pricing)
        var result = await _adjudicationEngine.AdjudicatePharmacyClaimAsync(evt.Data);

        // Cache result for pharmacy to retrieve
        await _resultCache.SetAsync(evt.CorrelationId, result, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5));

        // Publish adjudication result event
        await context.Publish(new PharmacyClaimAdjudicatedEvent
        {
            CorrelationId = evt.CorrelationId,
            EventType = "com.gainwell.pharmacy.claim.adjudicated.v1",
            Data = result
        });
    }
}
```

**Performance**:
- **50,000 events/second peak throughput** (morning rush)
- **1.2 second average adjudication latency** (within NCPDP requirement)
- **99.99% uptime** (4 minutes downtime/month)
- **Horizontal scaling** - add consumer instances during peak hours

**Scalability Approach**:
- Kafka partitioned by pharmacy NPI (evenly distribute load)
- Multiple consumer instances per partition (parallel processing)
- Result caching in Redis (sub-millisecond retrieval)
- Auto-scaling based on consumer lag metric

